<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy <span class="gold-text">Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: October 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section pt-0">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you create an account, we collect your name and email address. When you use the platform, we record your course enrollments and lesson progress so we can show your dashboard correctly. If you contact us, we keep your message so we can reply.</p>
      <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
      <p>We use your information to: operate your account, verify your email, manage your course access, track your learning progress, respond to your messages, and send important account emails (verification, password resets, course updates). We do not sell your personal data.</p>
      <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
      <p>We use a single session cookie to keep you logged in. It is HTTP-only and secure. We do not use advertising trackers.</p>
      <h2>4. Data security</h2>
      <p>Passwords are stored as one-way bcrypt hashes — we cannot see your password. Email verification and password-reset links are single-use, expire quickly, and are stored only as hashes. Course videos are served only to authorized users through protected links.</p>
      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may update your name and password from your profile page at any time. To request a copy of your data or deletion of your account, email support@earnwithalibhai.com and we will process your request.</p>
      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>This platform is intended for students aged 13 and above. If you are under 13, please use the platform with a parent or guardian.</p>
      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>If we make material changes to this policy, we will post the updated version here with a new "last updated" date.</p>
      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: support@earnwithalibhai.com.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

